  "notes": "Mongolian is boundary-matched, and because it is agglutinative a bare stem will NOT match an inflected surface form, so the high-value nouns carry their genitive/accusative forms (татвар / татварын / татварыг) and the verbs carry the -х infinitive plus the -сан past and -на future endings that headlines actually print. Deliberately avoided the bare generic verb 'гаргах' (to bring out/issue), which fires on ordinary prose, and used the collocations 'шийдвэр гаргах' / 'тогтоол гаргах' instead; likewise skipped 'худалдан авах' and 'нийлүүлэх', which are ordinary commerce rather than state action."
